        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Research Paper Page</title>\n<script src=\"https://polyfill.io/v3/polyfill.min.js?features=es6\"></script>\n<script id=\"MathJax-script\" async src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n<style>\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  html, body { margin: 0; background: #fff; }\n  body {\n    font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n    color: #000;\n  }\n  .page {\n    width: 1450px;\n    min-height: 1270px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    padding: 29px 22px 0 56px;\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 670px 1fr;\n    column-gap: 31px;\n    overflow: hidden;\n  }\n  .left { width: 670px; }\n  .right {\n    width: 671px;\n    font-size: 27px;\n    line-height: 1.185;\n    text-align: justify;\n  }\n  .right p { margin: 0; }\n  .figure-one { height: 283px; }\n  .fig1-art {\n    width: 650px;\n    height: 190px;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: flex-start;\n    gap: 39px;\n    margin-left: 13px;\n  }\n  .matrix {\n    width: 173px;\n    height: 174px;\n    position: relative;\n    border-left: 2px dashed #222;\n    border-right: 2px dashed #222;\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr);\n    grid-template-rows: repeat(8, 1fr);\n    padding: 1px 4px;\n    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 16px;\n    line-height: 21px;\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n  .matrix span:nth-child(3n), .matrix span:nth-child(7n+4) {\n    background: #070707;\n    color: white;\n  }\n  .heatmap {\n    width: 175px;\n    height: 177px;\n    position: relative;\n    border: 1px solid #bbb;\n    background:\n      radial-gradient(ellipse at 49% 49%, rgba(255,255,255,.94) 0 10%, transparent 21%),\n      radial-gradient(ellipse at 77% 45%, rgba(238,36,29,.83) 0 5%, transparent 22%),\n      radial-gradient(ellipse at 27% 58%, rgba(44,83,237,.74) 0 6%, transparent 24%),\n      linear-gradient(90deg, #273bc5 0%, #eef1ff 13%, #f6f6f7 36%, #fff0ef 61%, #e92920 94%);\n  }\n  .heatmap .nums {\n    padding: 0 2px;\n    font-size: 16px;\n    line-height: 43px;\n    white-space: nowrap;\n  }\n  .heatmap:after {\n    content: \"\";\n    position: absolute;\n    right: -22px;\n    top: 0;\n    width: 9px;\n    height: 176px;\n    background: linear-gradient(#ee1e18, #fff 49%, #1c2daf);\n    border: 1px solid #ccc;\n  }\n  .blob {\n    width: 173px;\n    height: 173px;\n    margin-left: 32px;\n    background:\n      radial-gradient(ellipse at 34% 32%, white 0 16%, transparent 17%),\n      radial-gradient(ellipse at 27% 49%, white 0 13%, transparent 14%),\n      radial-gradient(ellipse at 83% 51%, white 0 17%, transparent 18%),\n      radial-gradient(ellipse at 85% 91%, white 0 7%, transparent 8%),\n      #000;\n    border: 1px solid #777;\n  }\n  .placeholder { position: relative; }\n  .placeholder .hidden-caption {\n    position: absolute;\n    font-size: 1px;\n    color: transparent;\n    overflow: hidden;\n    width: 1px;\n    height: 1px;\n  }\n  .subfig-labels {\n    width: 470px;\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    margin: 1px 0 0 84px;\n    font-size: 19px;\n  }\n  .caption {\n    font-size: 21px;\n    line-height: 24px;\n    margin-top: 10px;\n  }\n  .fig2 { height: 246px; }\n  .fig2-title {\n    position: relative;\n    height: 41px;\n    font-size: 15px;\n  }\n  .input-label { position: absolute; left: 61px; top: 4px; }\n  .output-label { position: absolute; left: 409px; top: 4px; }\n  .down-arrow, .up-arrow {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: -10px;\n    font-size: 35px;\n    font-weight: normal;\n  }\n  .down-arrow { left: 25px; }\n  .up-arrow { right: 37px; }\n  .cnn {\n    height: 109px;\n    margin-left: 60px;\n    position: relative;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 34px;\n  }\n  .antenna {\n    width: 94px;\n    height: 61px;\n    border: 1px dashed #111;\n    background:\n      linear-gradient(90deg, transparent 16%, #111 16% 19%, transparent 19% 37%, #111 37% 41%, transparent 41% 58%, #111 58% 62%, transparent 62%),\n      linear-gradient(0deg, transparent 24%, #111 24% 28%, transparent 28% 47%, #111 47% 51%, transparent 51% 71%, #111 71% 75%, transparent 75%);\n  }\n  .stack {\n    width: 75px;\n    height: 63px;\n    border: 1px solid #333;\n    box-shadow: 7px -7px 0 #fff, 7px -7px 0 1px #555, 14px -14px 0 #fff, 14px -14px 0 1px #555;\n    background: #fafafa;\n  }\n  .smallstack {\n    width: 54px;\n    height: 38px;\n    border: 1px solid #333;\n    box-shadow: 5px -5px 0 #fff, 5px -5px 0 1px #555, 10px -10px 0 #fff, 10px -10px 0 1px #555;\n  }\n  .layers {\n    width: 52px;\n    height: 28px;\n    border: 1px solid #111;\n    background: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, #fff 0 4px, #111 4px 5px);\n  }\n  .outputline {\n    width: 55px;\n    height: 3px;\n    background: #111;\n    transform: rotate(-10deg);\n  }\n  .cnn-labels {\n    font-size: 15px;\n    position: relative;\n    height: 30px;\n  }\n  .cnn-labels span { position: absolute; top: 0; }\n  .lab1 { left: 170px; }\n  .lab2 { left: 370px; }\n  .lab3 { left: 537px; }\n  .fig2cap { margin-top: 1px; }\n  .left-text {\n    font-size: 27px;\n    line-height: 1.18;\n    text-align: justify;\n    margin-top: 23px;\n  }\n  .left-text p { margin: 0 0 14px 0; }\n  .equation {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr 38px;\n    align-items: center;\n    margin: 13px 0 10px;\n    min-height: 170px;\n    font-size: 25px;\n  }\n  .eqnum {\n    text-align: right;\n    font-size: 25px;\n  }\n  .equation.short {\n    min-height: 62px;\n    margin: 7px 0 9px;\n  }\n  .equation.gauss {\n    min-height: 76px;\n    margin: 8px 0 9px;\n  }\n  .indent { text-indent: 0; }\n  mjx-container[display=\"true\"] { margin: 0 !important; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n  <section class=\"left\">\n    <div class=\"figure-one\">\n      <div class=\"fig1-art\">\n        <div class=\"matrix placeholder\">\n          <span>0</span><span>0</span><span>0</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>0</span><span>0</span>\n          <span>0</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>0</span><span>1</span>\n          <span>0</span><span>0</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>0</span>\n          <span>0</span><span>0</span><span>0</span><span>1</span><span>1</span><span>1</span><span>0</span>\n          <span>0</span><span>0</span><span>0</span><span>0</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>0</span>\n          <span>0</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>0</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>0</span>\n          <span>0</span><span>1</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>1</span><span>0</span><span>0</span>\n          <span>0</span><span>0</span><span>0</span><span>1</span><span>1</span><span>1</span><span>0</span>\n          <span class=\"hidden-caption\">[Pixelated geometry matrix]</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"heatmap placeholder\">\n          <div class=\"nums\">1.00 -0.82 1.00 0.41 -0.69<br>-0.30 -0.57 0.83 0.69 1.00<br>0.92 -0.35 0.82 -0.74 -0.85<br>0.88 0.04 0.15 1.00 0.86<br>0.83 0.65 1.00 0.39 -0.38</div>\n          <span class=\"hidden-caption\">[Mapped matrix]</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"blob placeholder\"><span class=\"hidden-caption\">[NGnet-generated geometry]</span></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"subfig-labels\"><span>(a)</span><span>(b)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"caption\"><b>Fig. 1.</b>&nbsp;&nbsp; Geometry generation strategies. (a) Pixelated geometry and its mapped<br>matrix. (b) NGnet-generated geometry and its mapped matrix.</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"fig2\">\n      <div class=\"fig2-title\">\n        <span class=\"down-arrow\">⇩</span><span class=\"input-label\">Input: Antenna topology</span>\n        <span class=\"output-label\">Output: Antenna performance</span><span class=\"up-arrow\">⇧</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"cnn placeholder\">\n        <div class=\"antenna\"></div><div class=\"stack\"></div><div class=\"smallstack\"></div><div class=\"stack\"></div><div class=\"layers\"></div><div class=\"outputline\"></div>\n        <span class=\"hidden-caption\">[CNN structure diagram]</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"cnn-labels\"><span class=\"lab1\">Convolution+Relu</span><span class=\"lab2\">Convolution+Relu</span><span class=\"lab3\">Fully connected</span></div>\n      <div class=\"fig2cap caption\"><b>Fig. 2.</b>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; CNN structure used in the ML modeling process.</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"left-text\">\n      <p>antenna shape is expressed in terms of the linear combination<br>of normalized Gaussian functions, as shown in Fig. <span style=\"color:#073bd4;\">1(b)</span>. The<br>antenna geometry can be expressed as</p>\n\n      <div class=\"equation\">\n        <div>$$\n          \\left\\{\n          \\begin{array}{ll}\n          \\displaystyle \\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_i b_i(x)\\geq 0,\\quad \\rho_{\\mathrm{topo}}(x)=1\\\\[7pt]\n          \\displaystyle \\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_i b_i(x)<0,\\quad \\rho_{\\mathrm{topo}}(x)=0\n          \\end{array}\n          \\right.\n        $$</div>\n        <div class=\"eqnum\">(4)</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p>in which \\(b_i(x)\\) represents the normalized Gaussian function,<br>\\(w_i\\) is the weighting coefficient, and \\(N\\) is the number of<br>Gaussian functions. \\(b_i(x)\\) is calculated using</p>\n\n      <div class=\"equation short\">\n        <div>$$b_i(x)=G_i(x)\\big/\\sum_{k=1}^{N}G_k(x)$$</div>\n        <div class=\"eqnum\">(5)</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p>in which \\(G_k(x)\\) represents the Gaussian function with center<br>\\(\\mu_k\\) and covariance matrix \\(\\Sigma_k\\), expressed as follows:</p>\n\n      <div class=\"equation gauss\">\n        <div>$$G_k(x)=\\frac{1}{(2\\pi)^{D/2}|\\Sigma|^{1/2}}e^{-1/2(x-\\mu_k)^T\\Sigma_k^{-1}(x-\\mu_k)}$$</div>\n        <div class=\"eqnum\">(6)</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p>in which \\(D\\) signifies the dimension of input \\(x\\). In this case,<br>\\(\\rho_{\\mathrm{topo}}(x)\\) is mapped into a vector of hyperparameters \\(w\\quad=\\)</p>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"right\">\n    <p>in Fig. <span style=\"color:#073bd4;\">2</span>. The first two layers play roles in feature extraction,<br>and the third layer maps the extracted features into the final<br>output, such as the antenna performance at frequency points of<br>concern. The convolution layer is the fundamental component<br>of the CNN, which typically consists of linear and nonlinear<br>operations, i.e., convolution operation and activation operation.<br>The convolution operation introduces a small array of numbers<br>called a kernel to be applied to the input tensor, which is<br>an array of numbers. The elementwise product between each<br>element of the kernel and the input tensor is calculated at each<br>location of the tensor and then summed to obtain the output<br>value at the corresponding position of the output tensor, which<br>is called a feature map. This procedure is then repeated by<br>applying multiple kernels to form multiple feature maps to<br>represent the characteristics of the input tensors. Two main<br>hyperparameters define the convolution operation: the kernel<br>size \\(p \\times q\\) and kernel number \\(n_{\\mathrm{kernel}}\\). We suggest using a<br>\\(3 \\times 3\\) size kernel in the proposed algorithm.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:0;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;For overlap of the outermost element of the input tensor,<br>zero padding is essential before the convolution operation. The<br>kernels are shared across the entire image positions, which<br>largely increases the modeling efficiency by reducing the<br>number of parameters to learn. The outputs of the convolution<br>are then passed through a nonlinear activation function, which<br>is the rectified linear unit (ReLU) in the presented algorithm.<br>Then, the output is passed through the pooling layer to<br>implement the downsampling operation, which reduces the in-<br>plane dimensionality of the feature maps. Here, max pooling<br>is implemented, in which the maximum values in each patch<br>extracted from the input feature maps are outputted. The<br>used CNN consists of a stack of several convolution layers<br>and pooling layers, followed by one fully connected layer<br>and one regression layer. To achieve a balance between the<br>computational cost and modeling ability, a shallow CNN with<br>a layer number of 2 is recommended. The output feature maps<br>of the final pooling layer are flattened and connected to the<br>fully connected layer, in which every input is connected to<br>every output by a learnable weight.</p>\n  </section>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
